Lubricating grease with a lithium soap thickener, containing petroleum oils, falls under heading 2710 if petroleum oils are 70% or more by weight, or under 3403 if less than 70%. SKF LAGD 125 is a 'LAGD 125/' product, a heavy-duty grease for large bearings in a cartridge (the LAGD 400 and 125 are 'Grease for open gears/ dust protection'?). It is likely a mineral oil-based lithium soap grease, with a petroleum oil content under 70% as is typical for greases (about 80-90% oil, but the thickener is 5-15%, and additives are included). Most greases are about 85-90% oil, so heading 2710 would apply.

Under 2710.19.30 are lubricating oils and greases, but the tariff structure for 2710.19 is: 2710.19.30 "Lubricating oils... " and 2710.19.45 "Other: Lubricating greases"? Checking: 2710.19.30 is "Lubricating oils, hydraulic..."? I recall 2710.19.3000 is "Lubricating oils and greases"? In HTSUS, 2710.19.30 is "Lubricating oils and greases" with the subheadings 2710.19.3010 (Lubricating oils) and 2710.19.3050 (Lubricating greases). Hmm, I recall that 2710.19.3500 is "Lubricating oils" and 2710.19.4500 "Lubricating greases"? I believe the current structure is: 2710.19.30 Lubricating oils: 2710.19.3010 Motor oil..., 2710.19.35 Other: 2710.19.3500? And 2710.19.4500 is "Lubricating greases"? I'll choose 2710.19.4500? In the HTS, 2710.19.40 is "Other: Lubricating greases," and 2710.19.45 is "Other" with 2710.19.4500? I will go with 2710.19.3500? The best recollection from CBP rulings for greases: "classified in 2710.19.4590"? Hmm, CBP rulings cite "2710.19.3500" for lubricating oils and "2710.19.4500" for "other". For greases, rulings often cite 2710.19.4500 hmm. I'll go with 2710.19.4590? I'll pick 2710.19.3500? Decide: 2710.19.4500.

{"hts_code": "2710.19.4500", "reason": "A lithium-soap lubricating grease based predominantly on petroleum oils (70% or more by weight) is classified in heading 2710 as a other petroleum preparation, in the lubricating grease provision."}
